.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/
# anomalib's Engine writes its own run tree (results/Patchcore/fit/...) next to ours, with no
# way to turn it off that is part of the verified configuration. Untracked files there tripped
# the Colab sync cell's cleanliness assert mid-session. Ignore the lot -- results are large
# artifacts, not source -- except the reproduction record, which the VisA gate commits
# (results/reproduction/patchcore_ref_visa.md, protocol §2).
results/*
# NARROW, for the same reason as mvtec_ad2 below: the gate's reports live directly under
# reproduction/ and come in, but `<method>/<dataset>/maps|shards` must stay out. This was a
# whole-directory negation until 2026-10-02, when run_mvtec_ad.py and run_visa_secondary.py
# started writing method-scoped trees into it -- MVTec AD classic alone is ~1,725 test images
# x 3 seeds of native-resolution maps. test_results_are_tracked.py holds both halves.
!results/reproduction/
results/reproduction/*
!results/reproduction/*.md
# M3's per-category reports, same reason as the reproduction ones: they are the result, and a
# result that is not in the repository is a result nobody has. The negation is narrow on
# purpose -- `results/mvtec_ad2/<category>/` holds shards and native-resolution maps (24.9 GB
# across the grid), which must stay out. Only the .md files directly under mvtec_ad2/ come in.
# `tests/test_results_are_tracked.py` holds this: `git add -A` skips an ignored file silently,
# so a commit can carry a message describing a result it does not contain. That happened once
# (2026-09-21, vial.md).
!results/mvtec_ad2/
results/mvtec_ad2/*
!results/mvtec_ad2/*.md
# 2026-10-01: reports moved under <method>/ so two methods cannot pool into one directory
# (scripts/run_mvtec_ad2.py default_results). The negation stays NARROW -- one level of method
# directory and its .md files only -- because a whole-directory negation would sweep in the
# native-resolution maps, 24.9 GB across the grid.
!results/mvtec_ad2/*/
results/mvtec_ad2/*/*
!results/mvtec_ad2/*/*.md
.cache/
checkpoints/
.superpowers/
*.egg-info/
